# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Solve Case of the Gateway Express after exactly three creatures attack.
# Forcing: Three Savannah Lions are the only attackers, so one all-attack declaration crosses the solve threshold exactly.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no battlefield or hand, leaving no blocks, spells, or choices.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = the scripted acceptance observes the solved power bonus.
#   LOSE = the Case does not solve before the turn limit.
#   TIMEOUT = combat or the end-step solve trigger stops advancing.
# Card roles:
#   Case of the Gateway Express — solve lifecycle under test.
#   Savannah Lions — the three deterministic threshold attackers and solved-power probe.
#   Plains and Mountain — deterministic draw padding.
# Protocol path: attack declaration, solve-progress AbilityWordActive update, end-step solve ability, solved designation, and static power effect.

[metadata]
Name:Case of the Gateway Express Lifecycle
Goal:Survive
Turns:2
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Attack with three creatures and observe the Case become solved.

